{
  "story_id": "S023",
  "title": "Lonp1 loss induces a Ddit3-centered mitochondrial ISR-like amino-acid module",
  "status": "grounded",
  "rejection_reason": null,
  "exact_observed_result": "Lonp1 perturbation induced Ddit3 in 217 P MY Pineal Glut and 155 MB Glut and Slc7a1 in 217 P MY Pineal Glut. The same Ddit3/amino-acid state was stronger and target-engaged after Dnm1l knockdown in 151 TH and after Opa1 knockdown in 155 MB Glut, with Asns, Cars, Ddit3, Chac1, and Mars1 induced. Hspa9 guides induced an overlapping 151 TH stress state with Shmt2, Cyb5r1, Chac1, and Lonp1.",
  "biological_interpretation": "Perturbing several mitochondrial maintenance nodes converges on an ATF4/ISR-like amino-acid and one-carbon module in vulnerable neuronal classes, with Lonp1 contributing a smaller Ddit3-centered version and Opa1/Dnm1l/Hspa9 providing stronger comparator anchors.",
